{
  "en": {
    "description": {
      "tfm2_levi_levi": {
        "name": "Levi",
        "skill": "Cable: each press fires one cable that bites the first wall (or tower) along its line, up to 200000 away. At most two cables hold him: they steer him (mostly toward the newest), and when a third bites the oldest lets go. Every cable that bites during a flight is a Chain stack (the pips over his health bar) and adds speed as it connects: the most when the two cables he holds make a right angle, less as they line up or oppose (never under a quarter). Speed has no cap; his turning does: the faster he flies, the wider his arcs, and reaching a cable's wall fast (or any other wall) slams him into it, stunned longer the faster he was, unless the next cable bites first. Cables fire all the way round him: one that bites behind him whips him round to it (a turnback, losing a quarter of his speed). He flies toward where he's heading along the way around the walls, and lands to walk the last stretch. A cable that finds nothing breaks the chain and he glides down. Flying fast, he cuts enemies right in his path (15 + 25% AD, more the faster he is). Mastery (per athlete, from the games they have played on him: an official match counts 1, a scrim or exhibition 0.5, a win 1.5 times that; the badge at his top right) decides how seamless his flights are: Grounded (0-4 games) starts each flight at 2200 a tick, misaims 1 cable in 4, takes 1s to recover from a miss or a slam, grabs the nearest wall, fires the moment he can (no timing) and never brakes, so he hits walls; Tethered (5+) 2500, times the next cable (often a bit late), never fires at nothing, brakes before 1 slam in 4, escapes on cables; Swinger (15+) 2800, reads a cable's path for walls before picking it, aims for good angles, brakes half the time, chases on cables; Glider (30+) 3100, right angles, keeps his line, brakes 3 times in 4, gas on a cable; Skyrunner (60+) 3400, plans two cables ahead, always brakes when nothing can save a flight; Stormcutter (100+) 3700, reads further, near-perfect timing, air-dashes on gas where no cable reaches, wears a mantle of lightning; Comet (150+) 4000, perfect timing, plans two pairs ahead, becomes a ball of light trailing a mantle of white-gold flame; Apex (the ten with the most mastery on him, 300+ each, numbered #1-#10) 4300 to 4800, never misaims, plans three pairs ahead and keeps re-planning for the fastest line, with an aurora mantle and a rainbow halo. From Stormcutter up the mantle hangs from his shoulders at rest and streams behind him, dragged by the wind, when he flies fast or dashes. The higher the rank, the faster he swings round to a new direction (and a top flyer re-aims his cables at once when where he's going changes). With two cables he's pulled between them: from Swinger up he fires them in pairs, one to each side of where he's going (a wall or a tower each side), flies the diagonal between them without ever heading for either anchor, and fires the next pair as he passes; the higher the rank, the straighter down the middle. From Stormcutter up he hardly touches a wall, letting go and dropping onto open ground when nothing carries the flight on.",
        "skill2": "Gas (a tank of 100, refilled at once at home): on a cable, a boost of +600 speed for 8 gas, no cooldown; off a cable, a burst dash of about 40000 for 10 gas, every 3s. How well he spends it depends on his mastery.",
        "ult": "Rampage: for 8s he can't be crowd-controlled (a slam doesn't stun him) and every enemy he passes within 20000 is cut once per pass: 30 + 45% AD, more the faster he flies (up to 4x). Five enemies in a group, one dash: five cuts. If he's on the ground it opens with a sure cable toward the nearest enemy. Cooldown 60s."
      }
    }
  }
}